@startuml j10-several-shops
title J10 Several shops on one phone: add, switch, remove, import as a new shop (v1.1)
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam titleFontSize 17
skinparam titleFontColor #0E5C45
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #0E5C45
  LifeLineBorderColor #7FA89A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantBorderColor #0E5C45
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantFontColor #0B3D2E
  ActorBorderColor #0E5C45
  ActorBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ActorFontColor #0B3D2E
  GroupBorderColor #0E5C45
  GroupHeaderFontColor #0E5C45
  GroupBackgroundColor #F3F8F6
  DividerBorderColor #0E5C45
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  DividerFontColor #0B3D2E
  BoxBorderColor #0E5C45
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #0E5C45
  BackgroundColor #E8F2EE
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #B08A2E
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E6
  FontSize 12
}
actor "Shop owner" as Owner
participant "Browser UI\n(index.html)" as UI
participant "app.js" as App
database "localStorage" as LS
autonumber
note over App, LS : v1.1 add-on shops.js, through the window.Hisaab hooks of app.js.\nWith one shop nothing is stored beyond 'hisaab.v1'.
== Add a shop ==
Owner -> UI : open Shop settings; in the "Shops" block (#sec-shops) type a name, press "Add shop" (#shop-add)
UI -> App : click (shops.js)
App -> LS : park the current ledger: setItem('hisaab.shops',\n{ active, list: [ { id, name, data } ] }); the active shop's data is null
App -> LS : open an empty ledger: setItem('hisaab.v1', blank shop)
App -> UI : render(): the new, empty shop is shown
Owner -> UI : record entries in the new shop (J2)
UI -> App : save entry
App -> LS : save(): setItem('hisaab.v1', state)
== Switch ==
Owner -> UI : press "Switch" on the first shop ([data-shop-switch])
UI -> App : click (shops.js)
App -> LS : park the current ledger in 'hisaab.shops' (its data filled in)
App -> LS : put the chosen ledger back: setItem('hisaab.v1', chosen shop);\nits data in 'hisaab.shops' becomes null, active = its id
App -> UI : render(): the overview shows the chosen shop's total
== Remove ==
Owner -> UI : press "Remove" on a parked shop ([data-shop-remove])
UI -> Owner : first press: nothing is removed yet
Owner -> UI : press "Remove" a second time
UI -> App : click (shops.js)
alt two or more shops are left
  App -> LS : setItem('hisaab.shops', the list without that shop)
else one shop is left
  App -> LS : removeItem('hisaab.shops'): only 'hisaab.v1' remains
end
App -> UI : the removed shop is no longer listed in the "Shops" block
== Alternative: Import as a new shop ==
Owner -> UI : on the import card press "Import as a new shop" (#import-new)
UI -> App : click (shops.js)
App -> LS : park the current shop in 'hisaab.shops'; open a blank shop under 'hisaab.v1'
App -> App : the normal import (J7) runs into the blank shop
alt file accepted
  App -> LS : save(): setItem('hisaab.v1', the imported shop)
  App -> UI : the imported shop is open; the previous one is parked
else file refused
  App -> LS : return to the previous shop under 'hisaab.v1'; drop the blank one
  App -> UI : the import message gives the reason; the previous shop is shown
end
@enduml
